The carve-out is deliberate and narrow. We tell law firms that we cannot read
their work product. That claim rests on this code, and a claim about code that
nobody outside the vendor may read is not a claim a security reviewer should
accept. So the part that handles keys is open, and the drafting engine, prompts
and legal logic are not.

